  "description": "The month edit at :329-336 firing on its second condition rather than its first. SDTMMI arrives as '13'; NUMVAL-C accepts it and the store leaves it as '13', so IS NOT NUMERIC is false and it is the alphanumeric comparison SDTMMI > '12' that rejects. The comparison is on CHARACTERS, not on the numeric value, and :331 reports 'Start Date - Not a valid Month...' - note the capital M, which the sibling message at :340 does not have. Stage four is never reached, so CSUTLDTC is not called at all on this path. Expected values are STATICALLY DERIVED by reading app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl, its copybooks, app/bms/CORPT00.bms and app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD - never captured from a COBOL run, which is impossible in this environment (risk R-A). Java has no transient data queue, so EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') at :517 is reproduced through an explicit job-submission port; the eighty-byte content is identical and the dataset key JOBS names the TDQUEUE(JOBS) that app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:499-505 defines as RECORDSIZE(80) RECORDFORMAT(FIXED) BLOCKFORMAT(UNBLOCKED) DISPOSITION(MOD).",
